Description: Keep sticky floating windows in place when their output goes away
 When an output was disabled or unplugged, its sticky floating windows
 were moved to the centre of the remaining output, all on the same
 point, and enabling the output again did not bring them back. A sticky
 window on a workspace that also held other windows went along with that
 workspace, which is hidden when the focus was on another output, so the
 window was out of view and no longer followed workspace switches. And
 moving a workspace onto an output (move workspace to output) left that
 output's sticky windows on the workspace that was no longer shown.
 .
 Now, as in i3, the sticky windows of a removed output land on the
 workspace shown on the remaining output, at the same place relative to
 the area that windows can use there (the output without docked bars).
 Each one remembers where it was and goes back to that output when it is
 enabled again, also after several outputs went away in turn, unless the
 user moved, resized or swapped it in the meantime. A workspace that
 moves onto an output and is shown there gets the output's sticky
 windows. Floating windows that a workspace takes to another output keep
 their place relative to that area as a whole, without gaps.
